\f0\fs24 \cf0 *******************************************************\
* README FILE\
* AEM 7010 Project (Spring 2026)\
* Title: Unemployment Dynamics: U.S. vs Selected States\
* Author: Zachary Serby\
* Date: 2026-04-10\
*******************************************************\
\
*******************************************************\
* GENERAL INFORMATION\
*******************************************************\
\
* This project analyzes:\
* (1) State vs national unemployment dynamics using FRED data\
* (2) Skill-based unemployment gaps using IPUMS CPS microdata\
\
* Software used:\
* - Stata 19\
\
*******************************************************\
* DATA SOURCES\
*******************************************************\
\
* FRED series used:\
* - UNRATE: U.S. unemployment rate\
* - CAUR: California unemployment rate\
* - NYUR: New York unemployment rate\
* - TXUR: Texas unemployment rate\
\
* IPUMS CPS variables:\
* - EMPSTAT (employment status)\
* - EDUC (educational attainment)\
* - AGE (age restriction 25\'9654)\
* - WTFINL (final person weight)\
* - YEAR\
\
*******************************************************\
* PART 1: FRED DATA PROCESSING\
*******************************************************\
\
* Step 1: Import state unemployment data (CSV files)\
* - California, New York, Texas stored separately\
* - Saved as temporary files for merging\
\
* Step 2: Import U.S. unemployment rate (UNRATE)\
* - Merge state series onto national dataset by observation_date\
* - Keep observations within 2000-01-01 to 2026-01-01 sample period\
\
* Step 3: Clean and structure data\
* - Convert observation_date string to Stata daily date format\
* - Generate time variable for plotting\
\
* Step 4: Recession indicators\
* NBER recession periods manually coded:\
* - Mar 2001 \'96 Nov 2001\
* - Dec 2007 \'96 Jun 2009\
* - Feb 2020 \'96 Apr 2020\
\
* Step 5: Visualization\
* - Line plot of unemployment rates (US, CA, NY, TX)\
* - Shaded recession bands added using area plots\
* - Export figure as PNG:\
*   "Unemployment Rate Graph.png"\
\
*******************************************************\
* PART 2: IPUMS CPS MICRODATA ANALYSIS\
*******************************************************\
\
* Step 1: Load CPS dataset (cps_00002.dta)\
\
* Step 2: Sample restriction\
* - Keep individuals aged 25\'9654\
\
* Step 3: Construct labor market variables\
* - Employed = empstat in (1, 10, 12)\
* - Unemployed = empstat in (21, 22)\
* - Labor force = employed OR unemployed\
\
* Step 4: Skill classification\
* - High-skilled: Bachelor's degree or higher\
* - Low-skilled: High school or less\
* - Middle education categories dropped for binary comparison. Reason for doing so was because the project guidelines specified this.\
\
* Step 5: Apply survey weights\
* - Weighted unemployed: u * WTFINL\
* - Weighted labor force: lf * WTFINL\
\
* Step 6: Collapse to year \'d7 skill level\
* - Compute weighted unemployment rate:\
*   unemp_rate = u_w / lf_w\
\
* Step 7: Construct unemployment gap\
* - Reshape data wide by skill group\
* - gap = low-skilled rate \uc0\u8722  high-skilled rate\
\
* Step 8: Visualization\
* - Line plot of unemployment gap over time (2010\'962024)\
* - Export figure as:\
*   "Unemployment Gap.png"\
\
*******************************************************\
* METHODOLOGICAL NOTES\
*******************************************************\
\
* - All unemployment measures are weighted using WTFINL (CPS weights). Thus missing WTFINL from 2010-2020 cause no data points to be plotted for this period.\
* - Skill groups are restricted to avoid ambiguous education categories\
* - Recession periods are based on standard NBER definitions\
* - No imputation or missing-data interpolation performed\
\
*******************************************************\
* DATA PROVENANCE\
*******************************************************\
\
* - FRED: Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis\
* - IPUMS CPS: Integrated Public Use Microdata Series (University of Minnesota)\
\
*******************************************************\
* REPRODUCIBILITY INSTRUCTIONS\
*******************************************************\
\
* To replicate:\
* 1. Download FRED CSV files for UNRATE, CAUR, NYUR, TXUR\
* 2. Obtain CPS extract with required variables from IPUMS\
* 3. Run Stata script sequentially:\
*    - Part 1 (FRED merging + plotting)\
*    - Part 2 (CPS microdata processing)\
* 4. Output figures will be saved automatically\
\
*******************************************************\
* END OF README\
*******************************************************}